.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH collection 1  "collection " 
.SH NAME
collection \- Manage snippet collections: ordered runbooks you can share and run end to end with `fg run <collection>`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcollection\fR [\fB\-\-registry\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage snippet collections: ordered runbooks you can share and run end to end with `fg run <collection>`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR \fI<REGISTRY>\fR
Registry to talk to (default: the active login)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
collection\-list(1)
List your collections
.TP
collection\-create(1)
Create a collection
.TP
collection\-show(1)
Show a collection and its items in order (a bare name means one of yours; use owner/name for someone else\*(Aqs)
.TP
collection\-add(1)
Add a snippet (owner/name) to a collection
.TP
collection\-remove(1)
Remove a snippet (owner/name) from a collection
.TP
collection\-order(1)
Set the item order: list every item as owner/name, in the new order
.TP
collection\-visibility(1)
Change a collection\*(Aqs visibility
.TP
collection\-delete(1)
Delete a collection (the snippets are not deleted)
.TP
collection\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg collection create deploy
  fg collection add deploy anna/restart\-api
  fg collection show deploy
  fg run deploy
